merge that somebody else left half done",

208
00:15:28,451 --> 00:15:31,414
in exercises/m06-m10-integration.md.

209
00:15:35,254 --> 00:15:39,800
Answer aloud, without the table in front
of you. A strong answer goes through the

210
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:44,216
five operations in a fixed order and
gives each its proving file or directory,

211
00:15:44,256 --> 00:15:48,349
including the two forms a rebase can
take and the condition under which a

212
00:15:48,389 --> 00:15:50,896
cherry-pick or revert
has a second directory.

213
00:15:51,236 --> 00:15:56,416
It adds where HEAD is in each case, because
that's what an interviewer asks next.

214
00:15:56,456 --> 00:16:00,026
It names the files that look
like signatures and aren't.

215
00:16:00,066 --> 00:16:05,310
And it closes the loop: what git status
does with the same files, and why deleting

216
00:16:05,350 --> 00:16:06,535
them isn't an exit.

217
00:16:08,375 --> 00:16:09,302
Let's land this.

218
00:16:09,642 --> 00:16:14,642
An operation in progress is nothing but
files in .git; git status prints its first

219
00:16:14,682 --> 00:16:15,625
lines from them.

220
00:16:15,965 --> 00:16:21,314
MERGE_HEAD, rebase-merge/ or rebase-apply/,
CHERRY_PICK_HEAD, REVERT_HEAD and

221
00:16:21,354 --> 00:16:26,142
BISECT_LOG are the five signatures;
ORIG_HEAD and FETCH_HEAD are not.

222
00:16:26,482 --> 00:16:30,989
HEAD is detached during a rebase and a
bisect, and attached during a merge, a

223
00:16:31,029 --> 00:16:32,465
cherry-pick and a revert.

224
00:16:32,805 --> 00:16:37,799
Every operation has a continue exit, a
restore exit and a keep exit; the restore

225
00:16:37,839 --> 00:16:39,813
exits discard uncommitted edits.

226
00:16:40,153 --> 00:16:44,563
Before choosing an exit, find out what
was intended and anchor anything that was

227
00:16:44,603 --> 00:16:46,287
committed inside the operation.

228
00:16:48,127 --> 00:16:53,220
Read section 29.6. Then copy the table of
this video by hand, from memory, and check

229
00:16:53,260 --> 00:16:58,047
